     2	 * A thin HTTP entrypoint for the Metered Web Broker — one endpoint, one contract.
     3	 *
     4	 * The `Broker` is a library (see `packages/gateway/src/broker.ts`); nothing in
     5	 * the repo previously bound a socket. This file is the only "web" layer: it
     6	 * wires a `Broker` from environment config, serves `GET /health` and `GET /`,
     7	 * mounts the metered `POST /fetch`, and exposes the audit ledger at `GET /audit`.
     8	 *
     9	 * It uses Node's built-in `http` module (no Express) so the production image is
    10	 * small and cold-start cheap — one Node process, no PaaS, exactly what the VPS
    11	 * deploy targets. The broker's orchestration is reused untouched.
    12	 *
    13	 *   # run it (TS directly)
    14	 *   npx tsx packages/gateway/src/server.ts
    15	 *   # or, in the image
    16	 *   npm start
    17	 *
    18	 *   curl -s localhost:8787/health
    19	 *   curl -s localhost:8787/fetch -XPOST -H'content-type: application/json' \
    20	 *       -d '{"url":"https://api.example.com/wire/42"}'
    21	 *   curl -s localhost:8787/audit
